WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.370
Under the rule of Ei Sei,
the King who worked toward unification,

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.500
the Kingdom of Chin launched an
invasion of the neighboring land of Gi.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.660
Ou Hon, Mou Ten, and Shin:

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:52.370
these bold soldiers and aspiring
great generals were together here now,

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.120
ready to usher in a brand-new age!

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.410
Having assassinated many of
Mou Gou's thousand-man commanders,

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:04.660
Rin Ko fought one-on-one with Shin,
then vanished like the wind.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:08.000
But Mou Gou's army persevered,

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.660
remaining vigilant and
prepared for another attack.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.400
"The Great General at Midnight"

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.500
Shin?

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.410
Do you have a second?

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:31.200
You again. Can't stay away, eh?

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.910
Don't make that face. I'm here
because something's been on my mind.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:37.580
What?

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.450
All those commanders being killed...

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:43.250
You must have heard all about it by now--

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:46.000
did <i>you</i> pick up on anything?

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.540
Like what?

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:52.830
Like, how they were different from
the Gi troops we've seen so far.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:55.370
Different? Well...

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:00.330
There was this geezer-brat
who was sayin' all this random stuff

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.750
about the heavens or some such.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.120
A geezer-brat?!

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.250
Here I thought he was a
300-man commander, but get this--

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.370
he was a <i>general</i> !

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.290
Name's Rin Ko, Yan Koo, I dunno...

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.200
Whoa, whoa! He's a general--
at least remember his name!

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.750
Whoever he is, he's pretty powerful.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:24.000
And I get the feelin'
he was holdin' back with me.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.160
He's totally unlike anyone we've fought so far.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.620
Do you know about General Ren Pa?

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:37.830
Ren Pa? He's some famous
general guy, right? Strong and all?

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.910
"Strong" doesn't begin to cover it!

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:46.660
He's one of Sho's Three Greats,
as mighty as Chin's six great generals!

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.870
What?! Ren Pa was one of the Three Greats?

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:53.120
Ren Pa is currently in exile, in Gi.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:59.540
But as a former Sho general,
Gi's King Kei Bin doesn't trust him.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:02.370
So, in the three years
Ren Pa's been exiled there,

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:06.500
the King has never allowed him
to command the Gi army.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:11.120
The entire Middle Kingdom
believes Ren Pa to be out of commission.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.500
But what if that's all nonsense?

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:20.410
If the cool treatment of Ren Pa is a Gi lie,

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:23.700
we'll be stepping blindly into
a place where one of the Three Greats

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.660
is lying in wait.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:29.160
What? B-But then...

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:32.160
I see your intuition is still
the only mature thing about you.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:39.290
G-General Mou Bu!

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.830
Just where are you going, Ten?

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:48.870
F-Father! It has been so long!

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.540
I'm glad to see you're looking well.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.250
Father? He's your... You're father and son?!

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.120
Oh, didn't I mention that?

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:04.450
You look <i>nothing</i> alike!

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.790
Say, boy, what became of Ou Ki's poleax?

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:15.540
Still a little too heavy for me.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.580
Shin has Ou Ki's weapon?!

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.370
If you're never going to use it,
I'll take it off your hands.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:24.370
Yeah, right!

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:29.000
So, Father, what brings you here?

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.200
I didn't expect you to be joining this campaign.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.870
I'm here as Shou Hei Kun's messenger--

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:38.870
concerning the matter
you were discussing earlier.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:42.200
Shin... that general you fought

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.870
was working for Ren Pa--without a doubt.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:46.450
Looks that way.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.950
Which means...

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:51.450
...we're already caught up in his scheme.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:55.000
Yeah, but bein' up against
one of the Three Greats

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.500
is all the more reason why we can't lose!

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:07.120
May I, my lord?

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:08.910
What is it?

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:11.540
There is something I do not understand.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.950
My motivation?

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:16.290
Yes.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:19.330
Why my lord would suddenly rise up now,

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:22.080
after remaining silent for three years.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:27.290
Because he encouraged me to do so,
three years earlier.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:30.200
"He," sir?

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:33.540
One of Chin's six great generals, Ou Ki.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.500
I have not forgotten.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:42.000
Three years ago is when our Gi exile began.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.660
But you say Ou Ki suggested this?

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:51.950
That's right--you were traveling
between Gi and Sho at the time.

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:55.290
Did Ou Ki send you a missive of some sort?

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:59.700
Not a missive, no.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:02.580
The man himself appeared before me in the flesh,

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:07.870
at the residence provided to me in Gi.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:32.120
Ou Ki...

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.870
You know,

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:36.870
you always did have...

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:41.080
...this paralyzing effect on me...

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:48.000
You have my sympathies for your... troubles.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:48.030
"Ou Ki: One of 
Qin's Six Great Generals"

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:50.410
How good of you to come.

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:54.580
Come in--I have prepared good liquor,
like before a campaign!

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:57.160
I'll keep you here drinking for a full ten days!

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:02.080
Much obliged.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:09.870
Ou Ki had to cross borders
to visit me in Gi, exiled from Sho.

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:12.450
Along the way, he had
stuck his nose into a battle

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:14.290
between Go Kei and Lord Hyou,

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:18.580
so his visit had to remain a secret.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.500
Surprising, indeed.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:25.700
How happy you must have been.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:29.120
Yes--happy enough to bring tears to my eyes.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:30.500
But then again,

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:33.040
I cried plenty that night!

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:39.370
If Rin Shou Jo of the Three Greats and I

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:42.410
were friends who'd gladly
risk our necks for one another,

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:47.950
Ou Ki and his fellow generals
were my greatest, most hated foes.

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:50.040
But at the same time,
they were friends with whom I shared

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:53.370
suffering and joy alike.

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:57.500
So when the head of the six great generals,
Haku Ki, killed himself,

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:59.620
I wept,

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:05.200
and when Kyou was done in
by some dirty rogue, I shook with rage.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:06.450
Then...

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:11.120
...exactly how did
Ou Ki entice you, my lord?

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:15.540
All that blood-tingling, heart-pounding
action--it's all in the past.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:17.700
The world has grown so very dull.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:22.790
General, I understand your sorrow all too well.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.790
However,

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:29.000
if there ever comes a time
when you <i>will</i> take a stand,

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.250
let it be in battle against Mou Gou's army.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.830
That should prove a pleasant diversion.

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:39.450
Mou Gou--you mean...

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:42.620
that mediocre general?

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.370
Mediocre?

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.500
You've got that right!

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:54.080
R-Ren Pa is on the move?!

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:56.830
This isn't good, General Do Mon.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:59.790
Any castle <i>he</i> guards is practically impervious!

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:02.290
Even when General Haku Ki took on Ren Pa...

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:09.040
Now, now--no reason to panic.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:12.500
Ren Pa's arrival was not unexpected.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:16.790
My lieutenants have always had
plans in place to deal with him.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:25.120
It was good of you to tell me, my son.

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:29.410
Knowing this so early means we can
take our time building our strategy.

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:32.500
Seems today's war council will run a bit long...

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:34.950
Why don't I find us something to drink?

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:40.950
That's Mou Gou! He barely bats an eye
at the mention of Ren Pa.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.870
So Ren Pa is back...

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:55.790
Bluffing?!

00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:56.910
Yes.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:58.040
General Mou Gou?

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:00.500
It didn't <i>look</i> like he was bluffing...

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:03.910
This isn't the first time my father
has done battle with Ren Pa.

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:06.830
What? But... that can't be right.

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:11.330
You know that my father and I
are originally from the Kingdom of Se.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:13.330
Yes, but...

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:16.830
My father is of the same generation as Ren Pa.

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:19.870
As young soldiers,
they fought each other many times

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:23.580
in battles between Se and Sho.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:24.450
What's more,

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.910
my father has never won against him.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:27.620
What?!

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.040
No...

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:32.830
So when the path to becoming general
was closed to him in Se,

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:36.200
he was shunted over to Chin
with his young son in tow.

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:43.450
Father soon found success in Chin,
but never faced Ren Pa again.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:50.290
I doubt Ren Pa even remembers
fighting Father in his younger days.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:56.200
For my father,

00:11:56.200 --> 00:12:01.290
Ren Pa is one huge wall
that is simply insurmountable.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:07.030
"Mou Ten"

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:13.660
Mou Gou had a strange habit:

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:17.660
When he was under great mental pressure,

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:21.040
he would remove his general's armor,

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.950
transform into an old and grimy foot soldier,

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:25.330
and take a stroll around the camp.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:30.790
He would cap this off

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:36.410
by sinking back into a quiet field
and simply emptying his head.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:39.540
But that night...

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:46.450
Ren Pa... why him? Why now?

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:50.160
Still... hmm. Quite a nice moo--

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:53.040
Yesss! Dinner is served!

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:09.660
Sorry for stompin' on you.
Your nose stop bleedin'?

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:14.330
Hang on--lemme get you a little nibble.

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:17.410
You caught that rabbit, did you?

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:20.750
Yep! It's my dinner!

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:23.620
Our rations ain't enough to fill my belly.

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:27.620
Those higher-ups sure are stingy, eh, Gramps?

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:30.250
Here!

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:39.000
Whoa, Gramps--you're <i>huge</i> !
Who are you? And that beard! Wow!

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:45.000
Strange--I've never seen a
big old foot soldier like you before.

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:47.450
No?

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:52.540
I've never seen a youngster
foot soldier like you before, either.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.620
I'm no youngster foot soldier!

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:59.160
I'm Shin of the Hi Shin Unit--
a proper 300-man commander!

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:04.790
The Hi Shin Unit?
The special forces so dubbed by Ou Ki?

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:09.910
So this is Shin of the Hi Shin Unit,
who inherited Ou Ki's poleax...

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:11.500
Mmm- <i>mmm</i> !

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:15.750
So what're you doin' out here?

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.450
Well, er...

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:22.830
Just taking a little escape from reality.

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:29.000
Whaddya mean? Do old men
still have stuff to worry about?

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:33.870
Of course. With great experience
comes serious concerns.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:37.410
Well? Let this 300-man commander hear 'em!

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:42.200
All right, then. Don't mind if I do:

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:46.620
When I was younger, I never once
won a fight against this one fellow.

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:48.790
Yep, that happens.

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:55.080
Now I'm an old man,
and it looks like I'll be fighting him again.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:15:01.330
But he hasn't grown weak with age--
instead, he's in his prime.

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:05.540
Wow. Just think,
bein' that old and in your prime.

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:07.910
Mmm. He's a monster.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:13.080
Serious, right?

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:19.080
So an old man has to
take on this monster... hmm...

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:23.450
I don't see the point in worryin' about it.
I mean, you did it!

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:28.370
Boy... have you listened to a word I've said?

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:32.080
'Course I have!
You gotta fight this monster guy

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:35.250
you never beat before, right?

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:37.330
But you already did it!

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:40.040
Did <i>what</i> , exactly?

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:45.790
You got yourself the perfect
opportunity to turn the tables!

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:50.870
Okay, so the winner is
the last man standing, right?

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:54.290
This time, you win, then run
before he can even the score.

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:57.160
Then you'll have won the whole thing!

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:03.080
Whoa! You startled me!

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:08.330
You're right about that, Commander.
If I win this, I'll turn the tables,

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:10.000
and victory will be mine!

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:17.620
Y-Yeah... You show 'im, Gramps!

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:41.000
As you know, the recent attacks
have left us short some commanders!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.620
Those units will either
be led by their lieutenants

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:47.750
or be dissolved and
incorporated into other units!

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:50.160
Listen closely, Shin!

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:56.290
However, two thousand-man commander
positions remain open.

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:57.410
Therefore,

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:02.450
we will be promoting two
300-man commanders on the spot!

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.450
Huh? Did he just...

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:08.040
He said they're promoting 300-man commanders

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:10.160
i-into thousand-man commanders!

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:12.450
This is great, Shin! Now you can--

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:18.450
No, wait a second...
they said they're only promoting

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:21.370
two of them...

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:23.330
What's your take, Kyou Kai?

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:27.080
By rights, it'll be Ou Hon and Mou Ten.

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:31.830
Hey! What the hell?!

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:33.580
Now for those selected:

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:35.040
First up is...

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:41.870
...Mou Ten of the Gaku Ka Force!

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:44.660
You are hereby promoted
to thousand-man commander!

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:46.870
The Gaku Ka Force
will become a thousand-man unit

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.500
with an additional 700 troops!

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:54.410
You did it, Mou Ten, sir! At long last!

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:57.370
Eh. I'm conflicted.

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:59.040
Mou Ten...

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:05.330
What'd you expect?
He was at the thousand-man level already.

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:06.750
Yeah...

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:08.370
So...

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:09.790
...who's the other one?

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:17.500
And the second 300-man
commander to be promoted is...

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.000
...Ou Hon of the Gyoku Hou Force!

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:36.660
It was only natural you'd be chosen, sir--
in every sense of the word!

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:43.330
Bah! Figures it'd be them!

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:46.000
They <i>do</i> get good results in battle,

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.250
and they <i>are</i> nobility...

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:52.290
Are you all right, Shin?

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:54.410
I...

00:18:55.910 --> 00:18:57.290
I...!

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:00.830
Shin, sir...

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:02.080
Shin...

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:03.200
Commander...

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:04.660
You are dismissed!

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:05.660
Wait.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.250
My lord! What is it?

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:18.950
Shin of the Hi Shin Unit! Come forward.

00:19:18.950 --> 00:19:21.500
Shin! The general's calling you!

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:24.080
Shin!

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:26.910
Y-Yeah...

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:33.620
General Mou Gou--calling <i>me</i> ?

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:42.950
Huh?!

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:48.700
Y-You're that guy fro--

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:54.500
If we consider the sheer ability
shown by Shin of the Hi Shin Unit,

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.580
it is true that on this campaign,

00:19:56.580 --> 00:20:00.700
he is outshone by both
Mou Ten and Ou Hon.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:04.950
However, if we look at the prowess
shown in the past battle with Sho,

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:09.870
we see he has demonstrated might
beyond that of a 300-man commander.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:16.200
In other words, he is worth
creating a third commander's post.

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:17.000
Huh?!

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.000
What?!

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:23.660
B-But, sir... if we need another
thousand-man commander,

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:25.410
there are plenty to choose from.

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:28.790
Then there's the problem
of him being of servant stock...

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:31.160
What's the problem, exactly?

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:33.660
Er, n-nothing...

00:20:33.660 --> 00:20:38.620
This is an arbitrary decision,
made on a whim that is mine alone.

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:41.500
Accepting this promotion
will naturally provoke the ire

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:43.790
of those around you.

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:49.750
To silence their objections,
I must add a rather extreme requirement.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:51.870
An extreme requirement?

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:53.870
The enemy's head.

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:58.120
Specifically, the heads of three
or more thousand-man commanders,

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:00.620
or the head of one general.

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:03.500
If you do not deliver...

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:07.830
you will be demoted three ranks,
and must start again from corporal.

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:10.040
In short,

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:11.950
if you fail,

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:14.700
the Hi Shin Unit will be disbanded.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:20.580
Well? Will you still accept,
Shin of the Hi Shin Unit?

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:31.580
Like I said: That's nothin'
worth worryin' about, Gramps!

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:36.410
What impertinence!
How dare you speak to the general like that!

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:40.790
Anyone who'd back down
'cause he's afraid of failure

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:44.000
woulda been better off just stayin' home!

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:46.700
Startin' over from corporal? If I screw up,

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:50.410
I'll start over from the
very bottom rung--as a foot soldier!

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:55.370
What's more, I'm thinkin' bigger
than one lousy general's head.

00:21:57.250 --> 00:21:59.950
Shin of the Hi Shin Unit is goin' after the head

00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:02.620
of commanding enemy general Ren Pa!

00:22:10.250 --> 00:22:13.040
Mmm. Very well.

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:16.120
Shin of the Hi Shin Unit:

00:22:16.120 --> 00:22:19.540
you are hereby promoted
to thousand-man commander!

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:23.450
The Hi Shin Unit will gain 700 troops

00:22:23.450 --> 00:22:25.660
to become a thousand-man unit!

00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:35.250
We did it!

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:40.200
That whelp, a thousand-man commander?

00:22:40.200 --> 00:22:43.700
I'm sure he's strong, but he's still a child...

00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:45.870
Is he sure about this?

00:22:45.870 --> 00:22:51.040
My father's military skill may lag
behind that of other generals...

00:22:51.040 --> 00:22:55.580
but as a judge of character,
he is without equal.

00:22:57.160 --> 00:23:00.040
If that's who's recommending him,

00:23:00.040 --> 00:23:02.080
he should be fine.

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:31.370
<i>I'm dreaming of you, just like back then</i>

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:39.830
<i>Trusting, unafraid of anything</i>

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:48.080
<i>Your words that I always remember</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:56.540
<i>Are getting fainter,</i>
<i>mixed up, about to disappear</i>

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:01.500
<i>I go crazy trying to make them out</i>

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:05.830
<i>Barefoot still, I'd lost my way</i>

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:10.080
<i>It's okay to stop</i>

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>But even if I go after you,</i>
<i>if I hold out my hand</i>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Don't respond just yet</i>

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>But until I forget, don't change</i>

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.870
<i>I ask this of you, and yet</i>

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:34.200
<i>Like a long-awaited morning, it's starting again</i>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>And I still remember</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:58.010
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.020
"The Night Before Battle"
